-- title:
--   Weil constant times unit volume of the elliptic torus
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L$ an extension of $K$ of degree $2$, let $\sigma$ be a $K$-automorphism of $L$ such that every $K$-automorphism of $L$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma$, let $v$ be a nonzero prime of $\mathcal{O}_K$ and write $K_v$ for the completion. Let $c \in K_v^{\times}$ and let $\delta \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$ satisfy: the norm string $\delta \cdot \sigma_{\mathrm{GL}}(\delta)$ (the product of the first $\operatorname{finrank}_K L = 2$ iterates of $\sigma_{\mathrm{GL}}$ applied to $\delta$) is conjugate to the base change of the scalar matrix $c$, and $\delta$ is not $\sigma$-conjugate to the base change of any scalar, i.e. $x^{-1}\delta\,\sigma_{\mathrm{GL}}(x)$ is never a scalar matrix. Let $\tau'$ be a Haar measure, for the Borel structure, on the $\sigma$-twisted centralizer $T'_{\delta} = \{t : t\delta\,\sigma_{\mathrm{GL}}(t)^{-1} = \delta\}$, and let $u_0 \in T'_{\delta}$. Let $\gamma_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$ be regular semisimple, in the sense that $\operatorname{tr}(\gamma_0)^2 - 4\det(\gamma_0)$ is a unit, and elliptic in the sense that no conjugate $g^{-1}\gamma_0 g$ has both off-diagonal entries zero. Let $y_1$ be a norm conjugator for $\gamma_0$ and $u_0\delta$, i.e. $1 \otimes \gamma_0 = y_1^{-1}\,(u_0\delta)\,\sigma_{\mathrm{GL}}(u_0\delta)\,y_1$, and assume $T'_{\delta} \sqcap T'_{u_0\delta}$ consists exactly of the elements $y_1 (1 \otimes m) y_1^{-1}$ with $m$ in the centralizer $T$ of $\gamma_0$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$. Let $\tau_S$ and $\tau_T$ be Haar measures on $T'_{\delta} \sqcap T'_{u_0\delta}$ and on $T$, linked by the requirement that the push-forward of $\tau_S$ along $s \mapsto y_1^{-1} s y_1$ equals the push-forward of $\tau_T$ along $m \mapsto 1 \otimes m$. Then for every real $\rho$ with the property that $\int_{T'_{\delta}} w \, d\tau' = \rho$ for every nonnegative measurable $w$ on $T'_{\delta}$ with compact support satisfying $\int_{T'_{\delta} \sqcap T'_{u_0\delta}} w(st)\, d\tau_S = 1$ for all $t \in T'_{\delta}$, the following holds. Write $\theta$ for the real number attached to the push-forward of $\tau_T$ to $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$ of the set of $g \in T$ with $\mathrm{v}(\det g) = 1$ and $\mathrm{v}(\operatorname{tr} g) \le 1$, and $U$ for the $\tau'$-measure, as a real number, of the set of $t \in T'_{\delta}$ whose determinant is the image under $\mathrm{includeRight}$ of a unit $s \in K_v^{\times}$ with $\mathrm{v}(s) = 1$. If $T$ contains an element whose determinant has valuation $\mathrm{ofAdd}(-1)$, then $\rho \cdot \theta = U$; if it contains no such element, then $\rho \cdot \theta = 2U$.
--
--   At a finite place $v$ where the twisted object $\delta$ is of the second kind, the twisted centralizer $T'_{\delta}$ is the unit group of the quaternion division algebra over $K_v$, the determinant-unit locus is its maximal order's unit group, and the statement computes the Weil constant (the covolume of the elliptic torus inside $T'_{\delta}$) against the unit volume, the factor being $1$ in the ramified case and $2$ in the unramified case. It is the Weil-index half of the elliptic transport package used in the local comparison of twisted and ordinary orbital integrals for quadratic base change.
